A desktop-first workspace application built with Electron, Svelte 5, TypeScript and shadcn-svelte.

## Development

Requires Node.js 24, pnpm 11 and [Task](https://taskfile.dev/docs/installation).

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```

Quality commands:

```bash
pnpm format
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
task build
```

## Built-in shell

- Integrated title-bar tabs: open, activate, close, drag to reorder and pin up to 3.
- Pinned tabs restore when the app launches; `Ctrl+1`…`Ctrl+8` or `Cmd+1`…`Cmd+8` switch tabs, and `9` selects the last tab.
- Command launcher from the title-bar search button or `Ctrl+K` / `Cmd+K`.
- Pin or unpin commands from the launcher and Settings. Pinned actions persist between launches.
- Theme-matching right-click workspace menu with quick access to registered commands.
- Windows taskbar Jump Lists with native Windows icons, common actions, pinned workspaces and recent folders.
- Collapsible sidebar, status bar, dark (default), light and Solarized Dark themes, and persistent preferences.
- Typed, sandboxed Electron preload API for native folder selection and settings.

To add a command, edit `src/shared/commands.ts` and its handler in `src/renderer/src/App.svelte`.

## Packaging

`task build` creates a production bundle and an unpacked application for the current OS in `dist/`. The other Task commands create distributable installers:

```bash
task build:win
task build:linux
task build:mac
```

Windows packaging includes NSIS and MSI. Linux includes AppImage and DEB. macOS includes DMG and ZIP. Native packaging and code signing should be tested on each target OS.

Production windows disable Chromium DevTools, remove the DevTools menu action, and package only compiled application files and runtime dependencies. Electron Builder also disables Node debugging flags through binary fuses. Each packaging task audits the generated `app.asar` to ensure development files are absent. **Electron's built-in Chromium DevTools code is still part of the upstream Electron binary**; physically stripping it would require maintaining a custom Electron build.

The generated GitHub Actions workflow uses the shared Node CI workflow from `RuchirChawdhry/ci-workflows`. Running `pnpm test:e2e` requires a graphical session for Electron tests; the browser-only renderer test also requires an installed Playwright Chromium browser or `CHROMIUM_BIN`.

For Windows UI captures, install [Microsoft WinApp CLI](https://github.com/microsoft/winappCli), build the app, and run `pnpm test:screenshots` in an interactive Windows session. The visual suite opens each built-in app screen and writes labeled PNG files to `screenshots/`.
